Third-party notices for the container hook's bundle

Container hook version: 0.8.1

/usr/local/lib/billet/container-hook/upstream.js is the index.js of actions/runner-container-hooks v0.8.1 (the release asset internal/guestassets/container-hook.pin names by digest). @vercel/ncc built it as one file from that project's packages/docker and packages/hooklib, whose license is the LICENSE beside this file, and from the npm packages below, at the versions the tag's packages/docker/package-lock.json resolves. Each is reproduced as the license files in its npm tarball, read from a tarball that matched the lockfile's integrity hash, followed by the licenses of code those packages took from other projects. scripts/container-hook-notices.py writes this file.

The copyright comments the bundle keeps inline stay in upstream.js, which is installed unmodified.

